# Trivy CVE ignore list — surgical exceptions for vulnerabilities that cannot
# be fixed via package upgrade because Debian has not released a patch yet AND
# the package is a hard PreDepends of core OS userland (coreutils, apt, login,
# util-linux, bsdutils) so it cannot be removed without destroying the image.
#
# Unlike --ignore-unfixed (which silences all unfixed CVEs), this file lists
# each CVE explicitly with a rationale. New CVEs will still fail the build.
# Re-evaluate each entry when a Debian fix becomes available.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-04-10

# libsystemd0 — CVE-2026-29111
# Status: affected, no Debian 13 fix available
# Why we cannot remove it: PreDepends of coreutils ≥ 254, apt, bsdutils,
#   util-linux, login; removing it destroys the OS userland of the container.
# Mitigation: libsystemd0 is never loaded by our application (FastAPI +
#   Gunicorn); the CVE requires systemd socket activation which is not present
#   in a container environment.
CVE-2026-29111

# libncursesw6 — CVE-2025-69720
# Status: affected, no Debian 13 fix available
# Why we cannot remove it: libreadline8 → libncursesw6 is in the dependency
#   chain of the python3.12 binary itself; removing it would break the runtime.
# Mitigation: the CVE requires an attacker-controlled terminfo database which
#   is not accessible in our headless, non-interactive container.
CVE-2025-69720
